WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.732
A sequence lists individual terms in an indexed order

00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:11.138
Here the terms are one half, one fourth, one eighth, and so on, with each term half the previous one

00:00:11.138 --> 00:00:14.100
Their values approach zero as the index grows.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.333
A series instead adds terms, and its partial sums form another sequence

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:24.856
The first sums are one half, three fourths, and seven eighths

00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:31.433
Those sums increase even while the individual terms decrease, because each newly added term is positive.

00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:36.959
The gap from the partial sum to one halves each time

00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:43.490
After n terms that gap is one over two to the n, giving this exact finite-sum formula

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:48.100
Since the gap approaches zero, the infinite geometric series converges to one.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.667
The harmonic terms also approach zero, but their sum diverges

00:00:53.667 --> 00:01:01.773
Four terms from one fifth through one eighth each exceed or equal one eighth, totaling at least one half

00:01:01.773 --> 00:01:06.467
Every doubled block repeats this lower bound, forcing unbounded partial sums.
